  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing the Prototype**\n\nI\'m currently focused on replicating the \"Bra\" portal\'s functionality within a single HTML file. The aim is to create a fully operational, interactive clone using embedded CSS and modern JavaScript. My primary goal is to ensure a seamless UI/UX mirroring the original design while prioritizing efficient code for a single-file application.\n\n\n**Assessing Skill Requirements**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the frontend design skills needed. The goal is a production-grade web application with a rich UI/UX, institutional styling, and responsive layout. I\'m reviewing `frontend_design/SKILL.md` for guidance. The prompt emphasizes a single HTML file clone, so I need to decide how to best translate our Vite React project into that format, maybe by embedding or exporting.\n\n\n**Clarifying Project Structure**\n\nI\'m now grappling with the project\'s architecture. The prompt requires a single HTML file, which presents a challenge given the existing Vite React setup. I\'m exploring the implications of having the full app rendered within `src/App.tsx` and how to integrate that into `index.html`. Furthermore, I\'m considering whether `index.html` can function independently while also mounting `src/App.tsx`. I need to ensure all styling and interactivity, from Tailwind to Lucide, are correctly embedded or exported.\n\n\n**Defining Core Functionality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the essential features for the interactive UI. The goal is an ultra-slick, bug-free, and fluid experience. A \"Exportar C\303\263digo em Arquivo \303\232nico (HTML)\" option is on the table, allowing for direct rendering or insertion of the complete file into `index.html`. Users often request single-file HTML apps for easy copy-pasting or direct execution, which guides this development.\nI\'m weighing how to incorporate several features into the design. If we create a full modern React app in `src/App.tsx`, we can then include elements such as Lucide icons, responsive tabs, currency conversion, commercial intelligence charts, and more. Also, sound/audio feedback, Gov.br simulation, and more would be useful too. I\'ll need to figure out which features provide the most benefit.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_9195198989797848141"
