  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request Details**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the specifics of this user\'s request. My focus is on understanding the nuances of the desired \"Brapex Importa\303\247\303\265es\" clone, specifically the intricacies of creating a single-file web application with embedded CSS and modern JavaScript. I am clarifying the depth of UI/UX expertise required.\n\n\n**Refining the Color Palette**\n\nI am now focusing on the visual identity, specifically the color scheme. I\'ve pinpointed the primary dark green and background off-white, and am now selecting appropriate accent shades of light gray. Furthermore, I am exploring options for serif and sans-serif font pairings, aiming for an elegant and modern aesthetic that aligns with the \"Portal de Opera\303\247\303\265es\" theme.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Breakdown**\n\nI am now structuring the essential features to be incorporated. \"Intelig\303\252ncia Comercial\" and \"Radar de Mercado Mundial\" will be key \"cards de destaque\". I also want to include a currency converter simulating R$ to S/ (Peruvian Soles) and a menu of quick shortcuts. Finally, I\'ll need a way to present export products and their current prices, and visualize the complete export process.\n\n\n**Structuring the New Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial features. There\'ll be a section for document attachments, showing a \"Pending\" status for items like commercial invoices. There will be dedicated buttons for file attachment and a final \"GO TO PAYMENT (GOV.BR)\" button. Then, the payment section will feature a Pix simulation with a detailed breakdown (export fees, government emoluments, service charges), totalling R$ 245. The user will be able to pay with Pix, QR Code or Bank Slip. I am working on how to visualize a stylized QR Code display, the amount, and a \"Copy Pix Code\" button. Finally, I will add real-time tracking with tracking code entry. The interface will feature a route visualization (Brazil to Peru) with an \"Animate Route\" button, and a chatbot support interface.\n\n\n**Clarifying Code Structure**\n\nI am now focusing on the technical requirements, particularly the single-file structure. The instruction to write all code within a single HTML file containing CSS and JavaScript is key. I\'m exploring how Vite handles this scenario. I\'m considering writing a complete HTML version directly, and how React can integrate that into a `src/App.tsx`. I am now assessing Vite\'s behavior with standard HTML/CSS/JS in `index.html`.\n\n\n"
