  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Build Process**\n\nI\'ve been examining the build process, and it looks like `npm run lint` uses `\"tsc --noEmit\"`. The `npm run build` command is straightforwardly handled by `\"vite build\"`. I\'m starting to get a clear picture of how things fit together, particularly how React 19, Tailwind CSS, and Lucide icons work cohesively within the Vite framework to create a really smooth, appealing user interface.\n\n\n**Considering Dual Architectures**\n\nI\'m now wrestling with a dual approach. Can I successfully create both a robust, zero-error React application with modern tooling **and** a fully functional, single-file HTML clone of the Brapex portal? The initial structure seemed simple, but now I must consider how best to accommodate both demands. It is essential for these to co-exist without introducing unnecessary build complexity.\n\n\n**Generating Single-File Export**\n\nI\'m now completely focused on creating a \"single file export\" feature! The plan is to include a modal or download button within the app, providing a way to generate a complete `brapex.html` file of the full application. I think this can be done, the portal can be built inside the App.tsx file. I need to make the app capable of launching immediately into the full Brapex experience when run. I will now create an image to render for the hero section of the home page.\n\n\n"
