  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Styles for Index**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to best define fonts and custom styles within `src/index.css`. Considering Tailwind CSS v4\'s use of `@import \"tailwindcss\";`, I\'m looking into the potential of `@layer base` for base styles and utility classes. I\'m also considering font-family definitions in this context.\n\n\n**Establishing Color Palettes and Fonts**\n\nI\'ve established a root-level CSS variable structure for colors, aligning with the visual identity: institutional dark/light greens, sand tones, and an amber accent. Body styles now set the background and default text color, and I\'ve defined font families for different use cases: a modern serif for display/titles and a monospaced font for data, according to the project\'s precise requirements.\n\n\n**Implementing Responsive Layout**\n\nI\'ve specified `JetBrains Mono` for tabular data, perfect for NCM, currency, and tracking numbers. The focus has now shifted to full responsiveness, aiming for a consistent user experience across mobile and desktop. I am currently planning out the initial structure for screens and application sections.\n\n**Structuring Screens and Sections**\n\nI\'m now building out the application\'s initial structure, starting with the login screen. It has a header featuring a port/container background and the title \"BRAPEX: CONNECTING SOUTHWESTERN SAO PAULO TO THE FUTURE.\" Below is a subtitle/seal, followed by a \"Portal de Opera\303\247\303\265es\" card. I\'ve designed a \"Entrar com o Gov.br\" primary button with Gov.br branding. Also, I\'m integrating \"Ajuda\" and \"Suporte\" buttons for user assistance.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Structure**\n\nI\'m now outlining the principal dashboard, beginning with a personalized greeting, date, and operator status. I\'m focusing on \"Intelig\303\252ncia Comercial,\" detailing the imports and exports between Itapetininga and Peru, including specific products and a volume growth chart. I\'m also preparing a \"Radar de Mercado Mundial\" panel. I\'m also including contact information and a button to go between the login screen and the main dashboard.\n\n\n**Developing Currency Converter**\n\nI\'m now integrating a simulated currency converter between Brazilian Real (BRL) and Peruvian Sol (PEN). It\'s designed for bi-directional conversions with an adjustable reference rate (e.g., 1 BRL = 0.68 PEN). The interface features interactive inputs, instant calculation, and a breakdown of customs IOF (0.38%).\n\nI\'m also preparing quick access cards, linked to different sections or tools (documentation, shipment tracking, NCM lookup, and the currency converter).\n\n\n**Designing Export Product Section**\n\nI\'m now designing an \"Export Products & Quotes\" section. It will have a product search bar with category filters (Minerals, Agro/Food, Fisheries & Derivatives, Manufactured Goods) and interactive route toggling between Peru/Itapetininga and Itapetininga/Peru. I\'m focusing on a detailed listing of inputs with technical specs and supplier examples, like iron, copper cathodes, Peruvian garlic, and fishmeal.\n\n\n**Refining Export Product Section**\n\nI\'m now integrating an export process with selected items from the product listings, with associated NCM codes (e.g., 7200.00.00 or 7403.11.00) and descriptions. Each card will include an interactive button labeled \"Select for Quote / Process Export,\" that will auto-fill documentation. Details include a dynamic calculator for quantities in kg/tons, and interactive fields for origin/destination countries/ports, and transport modes, like road, sea via Santos-Callao. I am also working on a section for mandatory document uploads with visual status indicators.\n\n\n**Finalizing Document Uploads**\n\nI\'m now implementing the required documents section. I am working to make sure each upload has a functional \"Attach File\" button for each document (Commercial Invoice, Certificate of Origin, Quality Certificate, Bill of Lading). Each upload will feature drag-and-drop or click-to-upload functionality, progress bars, \"Successfully Attached\" status, and file previews. I\'ll also add a finishing button, \"GO TO PAYMENT (GOV.BR),\" with field validation.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n\n**Integrating Payment System**\n\nI\'m now integrating the payment options, first a PIX system with Banco Central\'s official standard, with a \"Copy PIX Code\" button (and a toast to confirm), and an expiry timer. I\'ve designed a \"Bank App QR Code\" step-by-step guide. I\'m implementing a simulated bank slip/GRU with a official digit line, barcode, and PDF download. I\'ll add a \"Simulate Payment\" button.\n\nI\'m starting a real-time tracking system. I\'ve built a search field and quick clickable codes, and a panel for shipment status and expected delivery, plus a route map.\n\n\n**Developing Real-Time Tracking**\n\nI\'ve finished the initial real-time tracking system with the South America map showing Itapetininga, Santos, and Lima/Callao. I\'m focusing on a dotted line representing the trade route, and I\'m adding an \"Animate Route\" button to simulate cargo movement with telemetry. I\'m also including a pause/restart control.\n\nI\'m developing an integrated NCM lookup table, with real-time searching on code or description. It shows import taxes and the Brazil-Peru agreement details. I\'m working on a multimodal freight simulation calculator to estimate transport costs.\n\n\n**Adding Support Chatbot**\n\nI\'m now integrating a support chatbot. It will have a floating button to open/close the chat, and an opening message to guide users. I\'m building automated responses for common queries, with quick-click suggestions. A user text input with the \"Enter\" key or send button are incorporated.\n\n\n"
