  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Translation Module**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing a bilingual translation module, aiming for a clean implementation within `src/i18n.ts`. My goal is to support both `src/App.tsx` and the `brapex_portal.html` file, including specific translations for \"Perfil do Usu\303\241rio \342\206\222 Acesso R\303\241pido \342\206\222 Alterar idioma\". I\'m thinking about how to best structure the data and handle context-specific translations.\n\n\n**Implementing Language Buttons**\n\nI\'ve decided to implement two side-by-side buttons labeled \"Portugu\303\252s\" and \"Espanhol.\" Clicking \"Espanhol\" will set the `lang` to \'es,\' translating every element across the entire application\342\200\224Screens 1-10, the navigation menu, and everything in-between. To clarify, the buttons will use a clear active state to differentiate the currently selected language, using appropriate background and text styling.\n\n\n**Refining UI Feedback**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI feedback for the translation module, specifically considering the replacement of `window.alert`. The goal is to provide a non-blocking user experience, especially within iframes. I\'m exploring inline toast/banner messages within the `.app-shell` to replace `alert` calls in `calcularFrete`, `copyPix`, and `CONSULTAR NCM`. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual feedback appears in `freteResultado` when the weight is invalid.\n\n\n**Expanding Translation Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the scope of the translation module. I will provide clearer feedback, particularly focusing on the button state, such as `\"C\303\263digo Pix copiado!\"` and its Spanish counterpart, and an inline NCM info card in `CONSULTAR NCM`. I\'m committed to maintainability and consistency, creating `/src/translations.ts` and updating `/public/brapex_portal.html` to ensure full-site language switching. I also need to double-check text across all ten screens, ensuring I haven\'t missed anything in Spanish, especially in the menu.\n\n\n**Expanding Translation Lists**\n\nI\'m currently updating the translation lists, focusing on the chatbot guide and user profile. I\'m also adding translations for the navbar items like \"Menu\" and \"Perfil do Usu\303\241rio\". On the login screen, I am adding translations for all text, ensuring full coverage. I will move on to the dashboard translations after that.\n\n\n**Adding More Translations**\n\nNow, I\'m working on adding more translations, specifically for the \"Radar de Mercado Mundial\" section and its associated content. I\'m focusing on translating text related to the economic data and product demands. Furthermore, I\'ve completed translations for shortcuts, translating \"Documenta\303\247\303\243o\", \"Rastreamento\", and \"Consulta NCM\" along with their descriptions. I also need to make sure to complete the \"Conversor de Moedas\" section.\n\n\n**Completing Further Translations**\n\nI am now focusing on completing translations for specific sections. I\'ve translated text for the \"Conversor de Moedas,\" including the calculation values between currencies. I am adding translations to \"Simular Frete,\" and completing translations for the Tracking Summary card. Furthermore, I have made progress on the UI elements for Tela 3 (Intelig\303\252ncia Comercial), incorporating translations for all text and headers.\n\n\n**Adding Product Translations**\n\nI am now focusing on translating product-related terms for Tela 4, including search bars and product lists. I\'ve translated product names such as \"Min\303\251rio e Adubos Minerais\" and \"Zinco e C\303\241todos de Cobre\" and also updated search prompts. I\'m also adding translations for export products and related phrases, like \"Principais mercadorias da regi\303\243o.\" I\'m carefully translating directional phrases, such as \"De: Peru \342\206\222 Para: Itapetininga\" to ensure accuracy.\n\n\n**Updating Documentation Translations**\n\nI\'m translating Tela 5, focusing on documentation. I\'ve updated phrases like \"Pre\303\247os indicativos,\" \"GEST\303\203O DE DOCUMENTA\303\207\303\203O,\" and \"Todo listo antes de iniciar el viaje.\" The checklist phrases are also done, and I\'ve added \"Confirmar Producto\" and \"FLUJO DOCUMENTAL DEMOSTRATIVO\" translations. I\'ve also added \"Processo de Exporta\303\247\303\243o \342\200\224 Item: Ferro / Insumos\". I\'m also ensuring all document descriptions are translated.\n\n\n**Finalizing Item Translations**\n\nI\'m now completing the translation for item-specific fields in the export process for Tela 5. This includes the NCM code, quantities, origin and destination countries, and disclaimers. I\'ve also translated all document-related phrases (\"Invoice,\" \"Certificate of Origin,\" \"Quality Certificate\") and their status indicators (\"Pending,\" \"Attached,\" \"Complete\"). I\'ve ensured all UI elements are translated too, such as \"Anexar arquivo,\" \"Nenhum arquivo selecionado\" and the CTA. I\'m double checking and completing the CTA: \"IR PARA PAGAMENTO (GOV.BR)\" / \"IR A PAGO (GOV.BR)\".\n\n\n**Translating Screen Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m translating elements on Tela 6, specifically payment-related items like \"Pagamento\", \"Boleto Banc\303\241rio,\" and various fees and totals. I\'m also addressing the Pix payment flow, ensuring that phrases like \"Copiar C\303\263digo Pix\" and success messages are accurate in both languages. Then, I will address elements in Tela 7.\n\n\n**Completing Simulation Translations**\n\nI\'m now focused on completing the translations for the simulation feature on Tela 8. I\'ve translated all the fields, like product, value, weight, origin and destination countries, and the simulation button. I\'m making sure all error messages are accurate in both languages too. Also, I\'m adding the translations for the tracking feature and the chatbot interaction.\n\n\n**Adding Tracking Translations**\n\nI\'m now translating the tracking module, starting with the tracking code input and button, including phrases like \"Digite o c\303\263digo de rastreamento\" and \"Rastrear carga.\" I\'ve also translated route-related text like \"ROTA ILUSTRATIVA\" and \"Brasil \342\206\222 Peru,\" including phrases about the animated route and the status indicators. Finally, I\'ve translated support chatbot phrases like \"SUPORTE CHATBOT\" and chat bot descriptions.\n\n\n**Translating Customs Guide**\n\nI\'m now on Tela 9, translating the digital customs guide. I\'ve handled the guide\'s title, introductory texts, and search-related prompts. I\'ve translated key phrases like \"Buscar por produto ou assunto,\" and example queries like \"certificado de origem ou alf\303\242ndega Peru.\" I\'m also addressing the \"Documentos de exporta\303\247\303\243o\" section.\n\n\n**Finalizing Profile Translations**\n\nI\'m now completing the translations for Tela 10, the user profile section. I\'ve finished the translations for the commercial and logistic documents. I\'ve translated \"Certificado de origem\" and its description, and phrases like \"MINHA CONTA,\" \"Perfil do Usu\303\241rio,\" and the account management prompts. I am also working on \"INFORMA\303\207\303\225ES PESSOAIS\" and fields like \"Nome completo,\" \"E-mail,\" \"CPF/CNPJ,\" and all company-related fields.\n\n\n"
