  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Missing Strings**\n\nI\'ve been examining `/public/brapex_portal.html` and noticed discrepancies in `I18N_MAP.es`. Specifically, key strings in the HTML are either absent or don\'t match up with their intended translations. I\'ve highlighted: `\'Conversor de Moedas\'` and `\'INTELIG\303\212NCIA ARTIFICIAL\'`. I\'m working to reconcile these issues.\n\n\n**Adjusting Spanish Translations**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining Spanish translations. I\'m updating several strings in `/public/brapex_portal.html`. Key changes include correcting terms such as `\'ATIVO\'` to `\'ACTIVO\'`, `\'Madeira\'` to `\'Madera\'`, and adjusting phrases like `\'Em rota para o Peru\'` to `\'En ruta hacia Per\303\272\'`. I\'m also ensuring consistent formatting, especially around the `\'\360\237\232\232\'` emoji, to account for potential whitespace differences in the DOM. I am also fixing a number of strings, such as `Milho` to `Maiz`, and a few that are already correct!\n\n\n**Refining Portal Interface**\n\nI\'m now implementing several interface improvements within `/public/brapex_portal.html`. This includes updating strings like \"Simular Frete\" to \"Simular Flete,\" and \"Selecione um produto\" to \"Seleccione un producto.\" I am also improving placeholder text, button titles, and replacing `alert()` calls with inline feedback, aiming for a cleaner user experience, just like in `src/App.tsx`. I will be checking duplicate keys in `I18N_MAP.es` along with the typo in `I18N_MAP.pt`.\n\n\n**Addressing Language State**\n\nI\'m currently focused on ensuring language state management works correctly in `screen-docs`. I\'ve realized that the `defaultValue` of input fields, like the destination field, needs a `key` to update dynamically when the language changes. I am evaluating whether using `key={`dest-${lang}`}` or controlled state is the better approach to keep user edits clean and prevent issues like `Peru` persisting as the destination when the language changes. I want the site to behave correctly for users.\n\n\n**Implementing Language Buttons**\n\nI\'m now implementing the language selection buttons as requested. The plan is straightforward: I\'ll include buttons labeled \"Portugu\303\252s\" and \"Espanhol\" to guarantee the user can always switch languages. This aligns precisely with the user\'s explicit request. The button text will remain constant as per the user request, regardless of the active language, ensuring clarity for users. I\'ve already confirmed the button labels are correct in `translations.ts`.\n\n\n"
