  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Request**\n\nI\'m focusing on the user\'s request to understand how to guide them to an external site. I\'m exploring the interaction with the \"entrar com o gov\" element and how to link it to the specified URL. I need to clarify the specifics of the initial screen interaction for precise implementation.\n\n\n**Identifying Relevant Skills**\n\nI\'ve evaluated the skills. It seems Firebase, CloudSQL, OAuth, Workspace, Google Maps, Three.js, PWA, Shadcn, and Figma are not relevant to this task. I\'m focusing on modifying the button in `/src/App.tsx` and `/public/brapex_portal.html` to link to `https://www.gov.br/pt-br`. I\'ve inspected lines 207-232 of `/src/App.tsx` and 388-406 of `/public/brapex_portal.html`. I see that the original was a button with an `onClick` that is replaced by an `<a>` tag with `href`.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation Strategy**\n\nI\'ve considered the implications of the new tab behavior. Implementing `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"` with the `<a>` tag cleanly opens the external site in a new tab, as desired by the user. I\'m confident this approach is the right one, based on the user\'s explicit request and avoiding the complications of `window.open` or unnecessary click events, allowing a smooth and efficient transition to the target URL. I am thinking the \"Entrar com o Gov\" button has no other requirement.\n\n\n**Clarifying Button Behavior**\n\nI\'m now investigating the potential implications of removing the `screen-dashboard` navigation from the \"Entrar com o Gov\" button\'s click handler. I\'m exploring the login screen and other buttons to clarify the dashboard entry. I am checking the `Ajuda` and `Contato` buttons, as those navigate elsewhere, to understand if this is related to their behavior.\n\n\n"
